ecorded</b>: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task &quot;Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show&quot; and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Not back</b>: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter&#39;s name and phone, at any hour.</li><li>Each moment has its switch, all on: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Booking start and end&quot;. The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-texts-a-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts a day</h2><p class="gd-p">Site health on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> has <b class="gd-ui">Texts today</b>: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>; iOS 16.4 or later).</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts, leads and hot visitors (customer service and Sales also get the last two).</li><li>Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.</li><li>Your own: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My phone alerts</b>.</li><li>On or off for everyone: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Phone alerts&quot;.</li><li>Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and <b class="gd-ui">My phone alerts</b> says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-lead-and-visitor-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead and visitor alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff get an alert, in the app and on their phone, for what needs a person quickly. They are never emailed or texted, so the daily email limit is untouched. The Admins always get them (every device that turned alerts on, so both of you on the shared Admin account); the rest go to the person it concerns.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Who gets it</th><th scope="col">Topic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A new renter lead: the contact form, the phone number box, a discount game claim, the live chat. It names the source.</td><td>You, and the person the lead is assigned to; if nobody, customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A request typed into the booking request or contact form and not sent (after the capture delay, 30 minutes)</td><td>The same</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A new owner lead, including &quot;Website form, unfinished&quot;, and again when an unfinished application becomes the 30-minute chase</td><td>You, and the Sales person it is assigned to</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A visitor turns Hot on Live visitors (analytics consent only, once per visitor per day)</td><td>You, and customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Visitors</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On duty means someone who had Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A lead alert goes at once, at any hour, unless the person turned the <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> topic off on that device (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My phone alerts</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">More than 5 lead alerts in 10 minutes become one &quot;N new leads&quot; alert for the rest of that window.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Test and verification accounts never get them, and a test address never makes one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The switches are under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts for leads and visitors&quot;, all on. Live visitors&#39; own &quot;notify hot&quot; switch must also be on for the hot visitor alert.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>customer service and Sales are only alerted while on duty. With nobody on duty, only the Admins are alerted; the lead is on Leads for the team in the morning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-everything-else-that-alerts-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Everything else that alerts you</h2><p class="gd-p">The same system covers more than leads. Each kind of alert is a rule with who gets it and a tier: urgent (phone at once, any hour), normal (phone, held until 8 am if it comes in the night) or digest (a line in the app and in the daily digest only). You get, among others:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A line when an important notice goes out to a renter, owner or investor: late return notices and return-time notice (urgent), payment links, balance overdue and payment failed (normal), a failed owner debit (urgent), offers, agreements, statements and payouts (digest).</li><li>The booking step by step: confirmed, car going out, car back (normal), closed (digest), no-show (urgent), offer sent (digest), offer expiring within the hour (normal).</li><li>Money: a payment of $500 or more, a refund paid (normal), the cash summary at 9 pm (digest).</li><li>Field jobs assigned and started (normal), finished (digest), running late (urgent). New reviews (3 stars or less is urgent), tolls and tickets (digest), usage over its allowance, new job applications.</li><li>A morning brief at 8 am (pickups, returns, overdue cars, open requests) and an evening wrap at 9 pm (money in, bookings made, problems open).</li><li>An urgent alert a team member did not open within 15 minutes comes to you.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Switches and amounts: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts for leads and visitors&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The App Store and Google Play links are empty until the app is published. When set, phones are asked to download the app instead of turning on browser alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The list of alerts is the table Staff alert rules (the assistant can switch one off); a few listed there are not made yet.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-also-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Also on your phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The tracker alerts (offline, left the zone or Ontario, speeding, driving after the return time, battery or unplugged), a scored AI interview, the nightly data health notice and a request to delete an account reach the Admins on their phone. Turn a kind off in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff alerts</b>; the levels (speed, hours offline, zone) stay in Tracker settings.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.

## Live visitors

1. Open **Live visitors** (customer service; Sales: **More sales**). "Live now" counts who is on the site now, "Visitors today" the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.
2. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.
3. Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone", the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit''s pages.
4. Suggested: the next step and a message. Press **Invite to chat with this message**, or **Edit the message** first. Sales can **Offer a 10% discount code** (one per visitor a week). **Assign to Sales** hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car** writes the message for you.
5. Press **Pages** for the whole visit. Press **Start a chat** to write your own short friendly message and press **Send**: the visitor sees it in a bubble.
6. A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago"), so check it before writing.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press **Name** on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press **Save the name**. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Follow-ups

Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours". Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.

Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.

## Live chat

1. Open **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor''s page, pages and signals, and the renter''s bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over** (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press **Send** or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.
4. **Hand back to the assistant** when you are done, or **Close**. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.
5. Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" or desktop alerts if you want them too.
6. A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (**Visitor left, no contact**); with one it shows **Follow up by text/email** and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.
7. **AI replies paused** at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.

> Tip: Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose "I sourced this client" on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.', 'Live visitors and live chat', 'Who is on the site, how likely each visitor is to book, one-click actions, follow-ups, the chat inbox.',
  'Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.

## Live visitors

1. Open **Live visitors** (customer service; Sales: **More sales**). "Live now" counts who is on the site now, "Visitors today" the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.
2. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.
3. Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone", the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit''s pages.
4. Suggested: the next step and a message. Press **Invite to chat with this message**, or **Edit the message** first. Sales can **Offer a 10% discount code** (one per visitor a week). **Assign to Sales** hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car** writes the message for you.
5. Press **Pages** for the whole visit. Press **Start a chat** to write your own short friendly message and press **Send**: the visitor sees it in a bubble.
6. A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago"), so check it before writing.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press **Name** on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press **Save the name**. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Follow-ups

Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours". Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.

Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.

## Live chat

1. Open **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor''s page, pages and signals, and the renter''s bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over** (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press **Send** or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.
4. **Hand back to the assistant** when you are done, or **Close**. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.
5. Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" or desktop alerts if you want them too.
6. A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (**Visitor left, no contact**); with one it shows **Follow up by text/email** and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.
7. **AI replies paused** at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.

> Tip: Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose "I sourced this client" on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.

## Alerts on your phone

With phone alerts on (**Profile** > **Phone alerts**) you get an alert, in the app and on your phone, for:

- A new lead assigned to you, or, when nobody has it, any new lead while you are on duty (live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes): contact form, phone number box, discount game claim or live chat. The alert names the source.
- A request someone typed into the booking request or contact form and did not send.
- A new owner lead assigned to you, if you are in Sales, and the unfinished application that became a lead to chase.
- A visitor turning Hot on Live visitors, while you are on duty.

1. Open the alert to land on Leads, Owner pipeline or Live visitors.
2. Call or text the person first; the task closes by itself when they send the form.
3. Too many? Turn **Leads** or **Visitors** off for a device on the same card. Bursts of more than 5 in 10 minutes arrive as one "N new leads" alert.

> Tip: Lead alerts come at any hour, so set your phone''s own quiet hours for the night.
